        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 25 at 2:48PM EDT until September 27 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Sustained northeast winds 20 to 25 mph, locally up to 30-35
mph. Wind gusts 40-50 mph, locally up to 55 mph.

* WHERE...Portions of southern Connecticut and southeast New York.

* WHEN...Until 6 AM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The strong winds will last for a very long
duration, possibly exceeding 24-36 hours. Considering the long
duration rain fall and full foliage of trees, impacts may be
exacerbated.

The highest localized winds are expected to occur on eastern Long
Island and southern New London county.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.

Secure outdoor objects.</instruction>
